			"fieldtype": "HTML",
			"label": "Condition Help",
			"options": "<h4>Condition examples</h4>\n\n<h4>Basic field value check</h4>\n<pre>doc.grand_total &gt; 10000</pre>\n\n<h4>Child table check</h4>\n<pre>any(i.expense_account == 'Capital Equipment - CO' for i in doc.items)</pre>\n\n<h4>Settings JSON</h4>\n<pre>doc.grand_total &gt; settings.approval_threshold</pre>\n\n<h4>Available names</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><code>doc</code> — the document being evaluated</li>\n<li><code>settings</code> — parsed JSON from Document Approval Settings</li>\n<li><code>frappe.utils</code> — <code>flt</code>, <code>cint</code>, <code>getdate</code>, and related helpers</li>\n<li><code>frappe.db</code> — read-only lookups (<code>get_value</code>, <code>exists</code>, <code>get_all</code>, …)</li>\n<li>Python built-ins such as <code>any</code>, <code>all</code>, <code>min</code>, <code>max</code>, and <code>sum</code></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Installed apps can register additional names with the <code>approval_condition_context</code> hook in <code>hooks.py</code>.</p>\n\n<h4>Field names</h4>\n<p>Use field names from the approval DocType. Find them under Setup &gt; Customize Form.</p>\n"
